// Phase 15 (Kaleam-structure rebuild) + Phase 16 (artwork completion
// audit) + Phase 17 (duplicate-slot promotion + unavailable-state UX
// polish) + Phase 19 (closing the 15 Category-B plain dot/circle items
// identified by Phase 18's source research): the Tashkeel panel's
// "calligraphic glyph library" -- a
// second, additional concept alongside tashkeel-library.js's font-
// driven OpenType marks (Layer 1, untouched by this file). This is
// Layer 2: a dense, style-organized library whose STRUCTURE -- 5 style
// sections in this exact order (thuluth, naskh, diwani, nastaliq/
// "farisi", ruqaa), each section's exact item COUNT and ORDER
// (42/31/32/20/14 = 139) -- mirrors a real reference tool's own
// Tashkeel panel, inspected directly from an attached, saved HTML
// capture of it (its #kaleam_svg_tashkeel container, .tool_row/
// .tool_col markup, and each item's own <g id="kaleam-tashkeel-*">
// naming -- see PHASE15_REPORT.md "Source of truth").
//
// CRITICAL, explicit correction from an earlier draft of this file:
// no item below is an invented/approximated vector redraw of a
// reference glyph, and none of Kaleam's own SVG path data was ever
// read or copied (Phase 16 also declined a later request to embed
// Kaleam's own extracted SVG artwork directly, and Phase 17 declined a
// later request to fabricate original vector approximations for the
// remaining unsupported slots -- see PHASE15_REPORT.md section 0,
// PHASE16_REPORT.md, and PHASE17_REPORT.md section 0). Every entry is
// exactly one of:
//
//   type: 'font-glyph' -- a REAL small-Arabic-letter glyph outline,
//     shaped by this app's own real HarfBuzz pipeline (glyph-shaper.js
//     + font-registry.js, the exact same code path used for ordinary
//     text) from one of this project's own already-licensed fonts.
//     Used for slots that are, by name, small-letter ornaments (a
//     genuine calligraphic tradition, reflected in the reference's own
//     "*-helya"/"small-*" naming -- حِلْية), OR (Phase 16, two Naskh
//     slots only) for a slot whose reference artwork visually matches
//     an already-used real letterform closely enough to reuse it (see
//     PHASE16_REPORT.md's provenance notes for exactly which, and why).
//     The letter field records the real character shaped; variationId
//     the exact already-registered font variation used.
//
//   type: 'font-mark' -- a REAL Unicode Tashkeel mark's real geometry
//     (fatha/damma/kasra/sukun/shadda/fathatan/dammatan/kasratan/
//     maddah/hamza/dagger-alef), extracted via this app's own real
//     tashkeel-probe.js (the exact probe Layer 1 already uses) from
//     that style's own representative licensed font. A real mark type
//     is assigned to one PRIMARY slot per style, plus -- Phase 17 --
//     any number of DUPLICATE slots that expose the identical, already-
//     verified geometry again (recorded via `duplicateOf`, pointing at
//     the primary slot's id, purely for internal provenance/audit).
//     This is never a fabricated second/third "variant" of a font that
//     only has one real glyph for that mark -- it is the literal same
//     path data, reused, matching the precedent already established by
//     Thuluth's meem-tashkeel-1/meem-tashkeel/meem-tashkeel-2 and
//     Naskh's naskh-wasla1/naskh-wasla2 (both Phase 15/16).
//
//   type: 'licensed-asset' -- (Phase 19) a REAL third-party icon asset
//     under a properly verified permissive license -- currently Google's
//     Material Icons "lens" glyph (Apache License 2.0; the actual raw
//     SVG file content was fetched and inspected, not just the
//     repository's license page), used for the 4 plain-circle items.
//     Never a font mark or font glyph -- the panel's detail text says so
//     explicitly ("عنصر مرخص", never "علامة حقيقية"). Full field-level
//     provenance (source, sourceUrl, designerCreator, license, licenseUrl,
//     attribution, modification/redistribution rights, the exact asset
//     file, visual-match assessment) is recorded per item in its own
//     `provenance` object, and in PHASE19_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md.
//
//   type: 'original-artwork' -- (Phase 19) plain, undecorated in-house
//     geometry (a symmetric rhombus, or 2/3 copies of it) created for
//     this project -- used for the 11 diamond/compound items among the
//     15 Category-B items, since neither a licensed circle-only asset
//     (Material's diamond icons are stylized gem/facet shapes,
//     explicitly rejected) nor a verifiable OpenClipart file
//     (unreachable for raw-content verification from this project's
//     environment -- see PHASE19_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md section 1) was
//     available for a plain diamond. Deliberately NOT modeled on
//     Kaleam's own (uneven, non-square) diamond proportions, and never
//     claimed to be extracted from any font or third party. Documented
//     the same way as licensed-asset items, via a per-item `provenance`
//     object with `source: "Original project artwork"`.
//
//     The 6 two-dot/three-dot compound items additionally carry a
//     `pieces` array (2 or 3 primitive copies, each pre-centered on its
//     own local origin -- see scene.js's addTashkeelCompoundUndoable
//     doc comment for why that centering matters) used for the real
//     click-to-insert behavior: these insert as a GROUP of that many
//     ordinary, independently-editable path objects sharing one
//     groupId, added in a single undo step, rather than one path with
//     multiple subpaths -- so the construction behaves as ONE Tashkeel
//     library item while staying made of real, separable vector pieces
//     underneath (Ungroup breaks it back into its individual dots,
//     exactly like this project's "Designs" library). Their top-level
//     `d` field is a merged preview path used only for the panel's
//     static thumbnail icon; the real inserted geometry always comes
//     from `pieces`.
//
//   type: 'unavailable' -- no legitimate production geometry exists
//     for this slot, and Phase 17 explicitly declined to fabricate one
//     (an original "structurally correct" construction was requested
//     and declined -- see PHASE17_REPORT.md section 0). Every remaining
//     unavailable item carries a machine-readable `reason` (never shown
//     to ordinary users verbatim -- the panel translates it into a
//     plain Arabic explanation) of exactly one of:
//       'font-gap'     - a real, standard Tashkeel mark type this
//                         style's licensed font(s) genuinely lack,
//                         confirmed in Phase 16 against EVERY distinct
//                         registered font file for the style, not just
//                         its default (Thuluth's maddah/hamza-above).
//       'no-asset'     - a generic dot/diamond/circle cluster
//                         construction with no real correspondence and
//                         no open-licensed equivalent found. (Phase 19
//                         promoted the 15 of these that had a genuinely
//                         verifiable source -- see 'licensed-asset' and
//                         'original-artwork' above; 6 remain, still
//                         genuinely sourceless per Phase 18's research.)
//       'unidentified' - an unlabeled decorative/hilya-compound form
//                         with no confident identification and no
//                         open-licensed equivalent found.
//     ('duplicate' was Phase 16's fourth reason category; Phase 17
//     promoted every duplicate-reason item to a real font-mark above,
//     so no unavailable item now carries that reason.)
//     Rendered dim/disabled with a small lock indicator and "غير متاح",
//     never substituted with an invented shape, another font's mark, or
//     a generically "similar-looking" open-license asset (Phase 16
//     searched for the latter and found none genuinely equivalent --
//     see PHASE16_REPORT.md). Its slot POSITION is still preserved
//     (never removed from the array) so the panel's overall density/
//     order/count keeps matching the reference exactly, per the
//     explicit instruction that a missing item is acceptable but a
//     fake one is not.
//
// Nothing here reads any SVG path 'd' data from the reference HTML --
// only its structural facts (section order, item id/count/position)
// were used, which are not copyrightable expression. Full per-font
// license/provenance records are in TASHKEEL_LIBRARY_PROVENANCE.md at
// the project root; Phase 19's 15 promoted items' full provenance is
// also recorded per-item below via each item's own `provenance` field.
//
// Current counts (Phase 19): 139 total -- 114 available (69 font-mark +
// 30 font-glyph + 4 licensed-asset + 11 original-artwork), 25
// unavailable (7 font-gap + 6 no-asset + 12 unidentified).
//
// Every available item is inserted via scene.addTashkeelGlyphUndoable()
// as a real, fully-editable vector 'path' scene object -- and the
// exact same path shown in its panel preview is what gets inserted
// (PREVIEW GEOMETRY == INSERTED GEOMETRY).

